he did like, a move.

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:34.530
He got like, wide, and then,

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:36.210
he was not afraid of me,

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:37.530
and he just started walking towards me

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:38.363
and it freaked me out.

00:06:38.363 --> 00:06:40.110
I was like, "I got a 5-iron here."

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:41.610
(audience laughs)

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:43.455
And he looked at me like,
'That's not enough club."

00:06:43.455 --> 00:06:44.642
- That's not- (laughs)
- Yeah.

00:06:44.642 --> 00:06:45.475
- And you're gonna need a bigger boat.

00:06:45.475 --> 00:06:48.630
- And I literally got into
a foot race with an owl

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:49.950
on a golf course in Atlanta.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:51.210
So it was pretty embarrassing.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:53.430
So that's what I thought
of, you know, for the-

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:54.825
- I really wish there was footage of that.

00:06:54.825 --> 00:06:55.658
- Oh god.
- Like,

00:06:55.658 --> 00:06:57.337
just the owl coming at
you and you being like,

00:06:57.337 --> 00:06:58.170
"Wait, what?"

00:06:58.170 --> 00:06:59.730
- My buddies wish there was, I know that,

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:00.673
because they were,

00:07:00.673 --> 00:07:01.860
I was really panicked.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:02.910
- [Kelly] Scream like little girl.

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:03.945
- I didn't know what an owl could do.

00:07:03.945 --> 00:07:04.778
I don't know what, you know.

00:07:04.778 --> 00:07:05.640
- I love owls.

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:07.110
- You do?
- I love owls.

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:08.940
- Did you grow up near them?
- And how I know they're-

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:10.290
Not really, but I just,

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:11.340
I own a ranch in Montana,

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:13.287
and they're big there.

00:07:13.287 --> 00:07:14.120
- Exactly.
- And they land,

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.080
and they, right in front of
where I put trail cams up,

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.580
and that's how I know they walk around.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:18.413
'Cause they walk around
- Yeah, I didn't know-

00:07:18.413 --> 00:07:19.560
and try to get stuff in the snow.

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:20.780
- Yeah, I had no idea.

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:21.720
But I always thought owls-
- They're huge,

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:23.640
They're wingspan are, they're massive.

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:24.660
- I just thought they were
intelligent, you know?

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:26.730
They got the little graduation
cap and the glasses.

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:27.571
I thought-

00:07:27.571 --> 00:07:28.500
(audience laughs)

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:29.670
- And very exorcist,
- Yeah.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:30.503
- Like, their heads go 'round.

00:07:30.503 --> 00:07:31.638
- Yes, looking around,

00:07:31.638 --> 00:07:32.471
the big eyes.
- Yeah.

00:07:32.471 --> 00:07:33.600
When their heads go around, it's crazy.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:34.530
- Oh, it freaked me out.
- Yeah.

00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:35.970
- His head didn't move,
and it was freaking me out.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:36.893
He was just staring at me,

00:07:36.893 --> 00:07:37.726
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:37.726 --> 00:07:38.559
- And I didn't like it.

00:07:38.559 --> 00:07:39.392
I didn't like it.

00:07:39.392 --> 00:07:40.225
(Kelly laughs)

00:07:40.225 --> 00:07:41.670
- So I hear this about your son,

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:43.140
he's musical, he plays piano.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:44.218
Right?
- He's crazy good, yeah.

00:07:44.218 --> 00:07:45.051
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:07:45.051 --> 00:07:47.040
Is anyone in your family
musical like that?

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:49.713
- Well, all my kids are pretty musical.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:51.870
I wish I was good, I can't-

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:52.703
- Keep him doing it, yeah,
- I will.

00:07:52.703 --> 00:07:54.000
I wish I would've done that.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.406
- He loves the classical stuff too!

00:07:55.406 --> 00:07:56.239
- That's, ugh.
- And I'm like,

00:07:56.239 --> 00:07:57.243
- If you can play classical,
- No, I'm like,

00:07:57.243 --> 00:07:58.560
- You can play anything.
- "Get off of that stuff.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:07:59.790
You gotta beat Billy Joel's career."

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:01.320
No, but no, that's,

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:03.150
training-wise, like, they
say that with singers,

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:04.350
guitarists, piano, anybody,

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:05.760
like, if you can nail classical,

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:07.680
you can pretty much
float through any genre.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:08.520
- But where does it go?

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:09.990
What do you do, you're
just playing like this?

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:10.823
- It's beautiful.

00:08:10.823 --> 00:08:12.630
- Oh no, no, we gotta make money.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:13.530
We gotta get out there.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:15.786
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:08:15.786 --> 00:08:16.904
We gotta...

00:08:16.904 --> 00:08:18.289
- Don't do it for the art!
- Yeah.

00:08:18.289 --> 00:08:19.122
(Kevin and Kelly laugh)

00:08:19.122 --> 00:08:20.400
No, he loves it, so.

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:21.233
- No, that's great.

00:08:21.233 --> 00:08:22.066
No, I'm telling you though,

00:08:22.066 --> 00:08:23.220
if he can do that, he can do anything.

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:24.180
- Yeah, well that's good.
- Yeah.

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:25.013
- Get into some blues,

00:08:25.013 --> 00:08:25.846
yeah.
- Yeah.

00:08:25.846 --> 00:08:26.679
- Yeah, all right.

00:08:26.679 --> 00:08:28.830
Well we have footage,
actually, so let's hear it.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:30.411
It's beautiful.

00:08:30.411 --> 00:08:33.494
(Kannon plays piano)

00:08:42.738 --> 00:08:43.693
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:08:43.693 --> 00:08:45.321
Ugh!

00:08:45.321 --> 00:08:47.278
I love it!

00:08:47.278 --> 00:08:49.050
It must be so cool to
like, enter the room,

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:51.000
and your son's playing piano.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.530
- It's fine, but what do you do with that?

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:54.480
That's all you, this is what you do.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:56.609
Show it on Kelly Clarkson.

00:08:56.609 --> 00:08:57.442
- No!

00:08:57.442 --> 00:08:58.680
That's like, a great outlet.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.480
Even if he never goes into music.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:01.860
- All right.
- Having that as an outlet

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:03.181
is so therapeutic.
- It is, it is.

00:09:03.181 --> 00:09:04.014
- He's good.
- Yeah.

00:09:04.014 --> 00:09:05.490
- And, again, all my kids are good.

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:06.960
So it's like,

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:07.793
it's pretty cool growing up with them.

00:09:07.793 --> 00:09:08.940
- But you have one son,
and is it three daughters?

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:10.883
- Three daughters.
- That's a lot of estrogen.

00:09:10.883 --> 00:09:11.716
- Woo!
- Yeah.

00:09:11.716 --> 00:09:12.549
(audience chuckles)

00:09:12.549 --> 00:09:13.382
- [Kevin] You're not kidding.

00:09:13.382 --> 00:09:14.215
- Your boy's gonna be built

00:09:14.215 --> 00:09:15.048
for a relationship.
- Yes, yes.

00:09:15.048 --> 00:09:15.881
- They're gonna force him to be ready.

00:09:15.881 --> 00:09:16.714
- I know.
- Yeah.

00:09:16.714 --> 00:09:17.547
(Kelly laughs)

00:09:17.547 --> 00:09:18.450
- It's on, it really is.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:19.283
- Yeah.

00:09:19.283 --> 00:09:20.116
You wrote a song!

00:09:20.116 --> 00:09:20.949
You said you weren't musical,

00:09:20.949 --> 00:09:22.560
but I heard that you
wrote a song recently.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:25.170
- I'm not musical, but
I love to think I am,

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:27.450
and I love to get out there and try,

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:32.250
and I partner up with a buddy
of mine, Mike DelGuidice,

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:33.600
who plays for Billy Joel.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:34.680
- Yeah.
- You know, in his band.

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:37.230
He's just amazing, and, you know,

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:38.850
so I'm always writing songs for him

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:39.683
and having him,

00:09:39.683 --> 00:09:42.180
he wrote, you know, a couple songs for me,

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:44.970
and it's just like, we just
go back and forth and play,

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:45.803
and I'll show up at a show.

00:09:45.803 --> 00:09:46.636
- See?

00:09:46.636 --> 00:09:47.469
But wait, you don't use it

00:09:47.469 --> 00:09:49.167
for anything other
purpose than you love it.

00:09:49.167 --> 00:09:50.010
You love it.
- That's true.

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:51.060
- See?
- That's a good point.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:52.200
- Yeah.
- You're right, all right.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:53.160
- You should listen to yourself.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.166
Okay.

00:09:54.166 --> 00:09:55.330
(laughs) You have good ideas.
- Yeah.

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:56.760
- Well, we need another break.

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:58.650
Kevin's special is called, "Irregardless,"

00:09:58.650 --> 00:09:59.670
it's a word, people.

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:00.840
It's on Prime Video,

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:02.917
and go online for info on his tour,

00:10:02.917 --> 00:10:03.864
"Owls Don't Walk,"

00:10:03.864 --> 00:10:04.923
but they do.

